    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Corbin Carroll** (77.71) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) as our primary drivers. **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a high-leverage spot in the two-hole against Phillips; his elite sprint speed remains our internal priority for stealing points in the scarce SB category. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a premium matchup against Rocker, where a favorable wind forecast (+5%) and a strong dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) push his efficiency well into the \"Strong\" tier. **Seiya Suzuki** (71.16) and **Josh Naylor** (69.80) are also excellent starts, with both players enjoying significant park factors (+14% and +16%, respectively) that elevate them despite the challenge posed by their opposing starters.\n\nThe lineup construction reflects a tactical approach to daily efficiency, though we must navigate a notable risk with **Cole Young** (52.70) and **Josh Naylor**. Both face a 42% rain risk in their matchup against Bradish, which could lead to a shortened outing or mid-game suspension. While **Cole Young** holds a decent score due to his leadoff position and favorable park factor, his value is throttled by a difficult SP matchup; he remains our most volatile start. On the bench, our decision-making remains straightforward today as the majority of our depth\u2014including **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Jose Caballero**\u2014are sidelined by league-wide off-days. **Mickey Moniak** remains unavailable on the IL, leaving our bench entirely devoid of potential replacements, effectively locking us into the current personnel. We are particularly mindful of **Dalton Rushing** (51.68) and **Alex Freeland** (47.93); while their scores are bolstered by the SP skill of Keller, their lower batting order spots dampen their offensive floor, making them the most vulnerable links in our daily pursuit of optimal Roto production.",
